{"kind":"request","text":"E4-B: the browser store keeps authorizations.\n\nE4 delivers the authorization port and a memory store. A browser\n`ScopeClient` needs `store.authorizations` in `browserCustodyStore`,\nand C4's browser form cannot compose without it.\n\nWork:\n\n1. `browserCustodyStore` implements the authorization port of E4,\n   in the database that holds custody, in its own object store.\n2. The order of E4 holds: the authorization write commits before\n   the custody write, and both run under the one coordinating\n   fence. A reload between the two writes leaves a permission mark\n   with no signing, and a retry stops `authorization-used`.\n3. Removal: the history of a key leaves in the transaction that\n   removes the custody record of that key, and at no other time.\n   State what the custody archive removes today.\n4. A database from before this step opens with no authorization\n   store. State the upgrade, and how the client reads a signing\n   that has no authorization reference (`legacy`, ruling\n   `34791662`).\n5. The bound of 64 positions for each key, with its stop.\n\nTests: the E4 authorization cases run against the browser store\nthrough the store's existing test double for IndexedDB. One case\nreloads between the two writes. One case opens an earlier database.\nOne control removes the order of item 2 and names the test that\nfails.\n\nOrder: after E4. It lands in the C4 head or before it, as you\nchoose. It adds no scope kind, no platform definition name, no\ncapability name or form, no tool family and no record model.","body":{"conditions":"browserCustodyStore implements the E4 authorization port; authorization write before custody write under one fence; removal only with the custody record; an earlier database opens; the E4 cases pass against the browser store; one control; one gate","target_head":"53aeda160c649117df1b591d192bd8eafb9ca666","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}